Performance and readability (2026-07 audit)
===========================================

Measure first (before code changes):

- Baseline Top-N packages with --profile: ctx_union share, dep-model hit rate, reprove counters
  (prover:test_stats_pkgs + stats:test_stats_print_ctx_union_*; A/B config:dep_model_cache)

Tier A performance (only if measured):

- Specialized/indexed feature_unification:unify or narrower heuristic:should_union_ctx
- Ranking overlap precompute + cheaper dep-model choice-sig (keep hazard-encoded cache key)
- prove_recursive ctx-changed path: reuse sorted OldBody; share helpers with prove_model

Tier B performance (if reprove-heavy packages dominate):

- Incremental prune_model / prune_proof / prune_triggers (avoid full AVL rebuild)
- Safer prover:learn store update (nb_setval whole-AVL deep-copy concern)

Phase A readability (docs/style only):

- Normalize chapter→section headers in Rules/*.pl (one ===== per file)
- Fix printer.pl module-doc paths; qualify "context" in hot comments
- Sync Handbook 11 submodule table with rules.pl; PlDoc gaps (rule/2, scheduler, unify)

Phase B readability (helper extraction, same semantics):

- Extract prove_recursive / prove_model case helpers
- Unify heuristic:strip_ctx onto prover:canon_literal
- Parameterize query.pl dep-model phase expansions

Validate:

- test_stats_pkgs + tinderbox-ng compare on vm-linux.local after any Tier A/B change


Emerge || / selection preferences still missing (2026-07, post-#112)
====================================================================

Context: Portage dep_zapdeps (lib/portage/dep/dep_check.py) uses ordered
choice_bins; portage-ng flattens most of this into ranking:prioritize_deps_keep_all.
Already mirrored: installed-first, newest-first candidates, same-CN newest
|| arm (#112), USE_EXPAND profile/target score, selected_cn / proven virtual
reuse. Source of truth for the emerge side is dep_zapdeps choice_bins +
intra-bin upgrade promotion.

High impact (real-tree || / slot / USE divergence):

- USE-satisfied before USE-change bins (unsat_use_*; || ( foo[a] foo[b] );
  demote arms that need use.mask / use.force flips — all_use_unmasked)
- all_in_graph: prefer || arm whose packages are already in the digraph /
  proof (beyond selected_cn + virtual proven-providers)
- Slot upgrade + want_update: for || ( pkg:N … pkg:M ), prefer higher slot
  under update/deep (llvm-style; emerge want_update / all_installed_slots)

Medium impact:

- minimize_slots / new_slot_count + overlapping-|| DNF (_overlap_dnf;
  fewer redundant packages; preserve ebuild order when DNF not needed)
- downgrade_probe demotion: avoid || arms that pull a lower version into a
  slot conflict / below highest installed-or-in-graph in slot
- Partial-installed fuzzy bins (other_installed / _some / _any_slot) when
  not all_available
- Virtual expand + zero-cost installed checks (_expand_new_virtuals)

Low / niche:

- Circular-dep demotion inside || (--onlydeps / circular_dependency map)
- Intra-choice cp_map consistency when several atoms hit the same CP+slot
  (emerge bug 600346)

Validate after any of the above:

- Overlay suite (esp. || / USE / slot cases) + tinderbox-ng compare on
  vm-linux.local; watch USE-dep || and llvm/gcc/python slot || packages
